-- petapp.sql — THE MASTER SCHEMA
--
-- Running this on an empty database produces a complete, current Leash
-- schema: 32 tables, all indexes and foreign keys, and the schema_version
-- journal recording the bootstrap scripts already baked in.
--
--   New server:        psql -d petapp -f db/petapp.sql
--                      then db/reference/*.sql
--                      then db/devseed/*.sql   (dev and test ONLY)
--
--   Existing server:   only the new db/changes/NNN_*.sql
--
-- GENERATED by pg_dump from a converted, seeded petapp_dev. Regenerate with:
--   pg_dump --schema-only --no-owner --no-privileges petapp_dev
-- ...and re-attach this header plus the schema_version rows at the bottom.
--
-- ⚠ After writing any db/changes/NNN_*.sql, update this file in the SAME
--   commit, then run db/verify.sh — it builds one database from this master
--   and one from the change scripts and diffs them. They must match.
--
-- Conventions, and why:
--   • Timestamps are timestamptz; pets.dob and the two availability .date
--     columns are `date`, because they are days and not instants.
--   • Money is integer cents everywhere. Floats drift under arithmetic.
--   • Enum-like values are text, validated at the API boundary — no Postgres
--     ENUM types, so a new value never needs a schema change.
